        "original_id": "e132e98b-90f3-58ee-a225-bc8f2315e0cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rachel Jacobs\n- Companies: ApprenNet, Amtrak\n- Events: 2015 Philadelphia train derailment\n- Places: New York, Philadelphia, Port Richmond, Washington, D.C., Pennsylvania\n- Roles: social entrepreneur, CEO\n\nFacts:\n- Rachel Jacobs was an American social entrepreneur and a CEO of a tech company.\n- Rachel Jacobs was born on October 3, 1975.\n- On May 12, 2015, an Amtrak Northeast Regional train traveling from Washington, D.C., to New York City derailed on the Northeast Corridor in the Port Richmond neighborhood of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.\n- Rachel Jacobs died at age 39 on May 12, 2015, in the 2015 Philadelphia train derailment.\n- Rachel Jacobs was commuting between her home in New York and the Philadelphia offices of ApprenNet when she was killed.\n- Rachel Jacobs had recently joined the educational technology company ApprenNet as CEO before her death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
